[I] Abstract video-game development language compiler

[T] avdl is a high level programming language and compiler for making video
[T] games. Games are described in an abstract way, and the compiler is
[T] responsible for turning that into an actual executable game for specific
[T] platforms such as Linux, Windows and Android.

[U] https://afloof.dev/avdl/

[A] Avdl Authors
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

